usage: cairn bundle [-h] [--db PATH] [--bundle PATH] [--pin PATH]
                    [--attest PATH] [--log LEVEL] [--json] [--force]
                    SUBCOMMAND ...

compile, pin and inspect the content-addressed gate bundle

positional arguments:
  SUBCOMMAND
    build          compile bundle/*.json plus the verifier script into the
                   gate bundle
    pin            record the gate bundle's hash in the operator-owned pin
                   file
    show           print the bundle hash, the pin hash and every (kind, hash)
                   row

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --db PATH        substrate SQLite file
  --bundle PATH    gate bundle SQLite file
  --pin PATH       gate-bundle pin file
  --attest PATH    attestation file
  --log LEVEL      log level for the JSON records on stderr
  --json, --robot  emit exactly one JSON document on stdout
  --force          required for the irreversible part of this command

Structured output: add --json to any read-side command. Contract: cairn
capabilities --json. Agent handbook: cairn robot-docs.
